Version: 1.0
desc: All Ears Binauraliser (SPARTA Binauraliser port) by chmaha
tags: spatial binaural hrtf headphones 3d panner
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Places up to 64 input channels around the listener on headphones with head-related transfer functions (HRTFs).
  Each input is a source with its own azimuth and elevation; the HRTF for a direction is interpolated from the
  three nearest measurements of a KEMAR dummy head (Genelec Aural ID, 836 directions) inside an alias-free
  filterbank. Scene rotation (yaw, pitch, roll) suits head-tracking, diffuse-field equalisation flattens the
  overall timbre, and the loudspeaker presets drop the sources onto common layouts from stereo to 22.2, including
  5.1 to 7.1.4 in L R C LFE order with the LFE channel fed to both ears.
  Ported from SPARTA Binauraliser and the Spatial_Audio_Framework by Leo McCormack
  https://github.com/leomccormack/SPARTA (GPL-3.0), https://github.com/leomccormack/Spatial_Audio_Framework (ISC)
  afSTFT filterbank by Juha Vilkamo (MIT); HRIRs: Genelec Aural ID of a KEMAR dummy head, kindly provided by
  Aki Mäkivirta and Jaan Johansson (ISC, see Dependencies/AllEars/AllEars-LICENSE.txt)
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0 license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/AllEars/hrtf.txt
  Dependencies/AllEars/AllEars-LICENSE.txt

